    "text": "By Stacy Ryburn ,\n14 hours ago FAYETTEVILLE — South School Avenue south of Martin Luther King Jr. Boulevard should have two car lanes reduced in favor of on-street parking, street trees and public seating, a City Council committee recommended last week. The council’s Transportation Committee on Jan. 27 weighed in on some conceptual designs made... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
